---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import researchers from '../data/doctoral-research.json';
import '../styles/lab-teaching.css';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Lab"
  description="AI systems in the field and the organization of human–AI work. Research methods and doctoral research in Daniel Heinz’s lab at KIT."
  active="lab"
  bodyClass="lab-teaching-page"
>
  <nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Back to home">
    <a href="/"><Arrow /> Home</a>
  </nav>

  <h1>Lab</h1>
  <p class="lede">We study how work gets organized when AI agents act in firms, in new ventures, and between organizations. We design, build, and evaluate AI systems in the field.</p>

  <section class="field-section" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
    <h2 id="practice-title">Research from inside the work</h2>
    <p>How does an AI system become part of everyday operations? Who decides what, and what do people need to learn? Building a system gives us a way to examine these questions as the work changes.</p>

    <dl class="practice-sequence">
      <div><dt>Observe</dt><dd>Use qualitative research, including interviews, case studies, and taxonomies, alongside computationally intensive theory construction to generate hypotheses.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Build</dt><dd>Use design science to develop AI-based interventions and deploy them in organizations and ventures.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Test</dt><dd>Evaluate the interventions through field experiments and interviews.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Teach</dt><dd>Bring the questions and methods into courses where students build and test their own ideas.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="field-section" aria-labelledby="doctoral-title">
    <h2 id="doctoral-title">Doctoral research</h2>
    <p>I provide day-to-day research advising for Jonas Liebschner, Linda Sagnier Eckert, and Ida Meier. Prof. Gerhard Satzger provides formal doctoral supervision for these three researchers.</p>
    <div class="doctoral-projects">
      {researchers.map(researcher => (
        <article class="doctoral-project">
          <img class="researcher-portrait" src={researcher.portrait.src} width={researcher.portrait.width} height={researcher.portrait.height} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <h3>{researcher.topic}</h3>
          <p class="research-question">{researcher.question}</p>
          <p class="researcher"><a href={researcher.url}>{researcher.name}</a><span>{researcher.since}</span></p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="portrait-credit">Portraits: KIT, from the linked researcher profiles and arrival announcement. <a href="https://dsi.win.kit.edu/legals.php">Reuse terms</a>.</p>
    <p>These questions also connect to our <a href="/at-a-glance/#funded-projects">funded research projects</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="field-section" aria-labelledby="instrument-title">
    <h2 id="instrument-title">A system we learn from</h2>
    <p>Our AI-based venture tool helps early-stage founders structure their venture and examine the assumptions behind it. We use it in KIT coaching formats and as an instrument for studying entrepreneurial judgment.</p>
    <a class="text-link section-link" href="/tools/">Tools in use <Arrow /></a>
  </section>

  <section class="field-section" aria-labelledby="kit-title">
    <h2 id="kit-title">At KIT</h2>
    <p>I lead the Digital Service Design &amp; Innovation Lab at Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, within the DSI-WI4 team. Our research connects service innovation, data ecosystems, and the organization of human–AI work.</p>
    <a class="text-link section-link" href="https://dsi.win.kit.edu/dsdi.php">Meet the lab at KIT <Arrow /></a>
  </section>

  <nav class="related-pages" aria-label="Continue exploring">
    <a class="text-link" href="/research/">Research <Arrow /></a>
    <a class="text-link" href="/teaching/">Teaching <Arrow /></a>
  </nav>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .portrait-credit { font-size: 14px; color: var(--mute); }
  .doctoral-projects { container-type: inline-size; }
  .doctoral-project {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 104px minmax(0, 1fr);
    grid-template-areas: "portrait topic" "portrait question" "portrait researcher";
    gap: 12px 24px;
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .researcher-portrait {
    grid-area: portrait;
    width: 104px;
    height: 104px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .doctoral-project h3 { grid-area: topic; font-size: 16px; }
  .research-question { grid-area: question; }
  .researcher { grid-area: researcher; color: var(--mute); }
  .researcher span { display: block; }

  @container (max-width: 420px) {
    .doctoral-project {
      grid-template-columns: 72px minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-areas: "portrait researcher" "topic topic" "question question";
      column-gap: 16px;
    }
    .researcher-portrait { width: 72px; height: 72px; }
    .researcher { align-self: center; }
    .doctoral-project h3 { margin-top: 4px; }
  }
</style>
